course: dictionary
lesson: 3047
title: One word, many meanings: ease
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word ease can mean several things, so context tells you which one. Read the words around it and ask which meaning fits. «Doctors save many lives and ease pain» means they make pain less, not that the pain is easy.
explain: Ease can mean doing something with no difficulty. «She solved the puzzle with ease» means she solved it easily. Ease can also mean a calm, comfortable feeling. A child who is «at ease» is relaxed and not worried.
explain: Ease can also be a verb for moving things. To ease something is to move it slowly and carefully, like easing a splinter out of your finger. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense.
fact: Ease means doing something with no difficulty, or a calm, relaxed, comfortable feeling.
fact: To ease is to make pain, worry or a problem less.
fact: To ease something is to move it slowly and carefully.
fact: «At ease» means relaxed, and «with ease» means easily.
fact: «A dull ache that eases in a few days» means the ache gets less over a few days.
exercise: «She solved the puzzle with ease.» What does with ease mean? | Loudly | Very slowly and carefully | Angrily | *Easily, with no difficulty
exercise: «Doctors save many lives and ease pain.» What does ease mean here? | Forget about the pain | *Make the pain less | Make the pain stronger | Move the pain somewhere else
exercise: «Ben felt at ease in his new class.» What does at ease mean? | Lost and confused | Angry and loud | Ready to run away | *Relaxed and comfortable
test: You ease a splinter out of your finger. What does ease mean here? | *Move it slowly and carefully | Forget where it is | Make the splinter bigger | Throw it away quickly
test: «The warm drink helped ease her worry.» What does ease mean here? | Ask her why she is worried | *Make her worry less | Hide her worry | Add to her worry
exam: Sam says ease always means easy. Read «The medicine will ease the ache.» What does ease mean in this sentence? | *Make the ache less | Make the ache last longer | Be easy to swallow | Ache very badly
